1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:05,290
Turning a page requires more than moving a fingertip through the right trajectory.
翻页不只是让指尖经过正确轨迹。

2
00:00:05,930 --> 00:00:11,030
The robot must separate the paper and regulate contact without picking up several sheets.
机器人还要分离纸页，避免同时带起多页。

3
00:00:11,628 --> 00:00:19,088
UVTA records synchronized images, tactile signals, wrist pose, and hand motion during human demonstrations.
UVTA同步记录人类图像、触觉、腕姿和手部运动。

4
00:00:19,608 --> 00:00:25,228
A tactile motion-capture apparatus makes the contact evidence available alongside the visible action.
触觉动捕装置让可见动作拥有对应接触证据。

5
00:00:25,829 --> 00:00:30,849
Human and robot sensing enter an aligned visual-tactile interaction representation.
人类和机器人感知进入对齐的视触觉交互表征。

6
00:00:31,369 --> 00:00:36,529
The purpose is to share useful interaction structure while retaining actions suitable for each embodiment.
目标是共享交互规律，同时保留各手型适用的动作。

7
00:00:37,435 --> 00:00:43,455
The model jointly predicts future action trajectories and future tactile trajectories during training.
训练时，模型联合预测未来动作轨迹和触觉轨迹。

8
00:00:44,015 --> 00:00:49,815
This auxiliary tactile objective encourages the representation to encode what an action should feel like.
辅助触觉目标促使表征理解动作应产生怎样的接触。

9
00:00:50,327 --> 00:00:56,427
Future tactile prediction helps train the model; it is not a separate deployed controller output.
未来触觉预测用于训练，并非独立部署控制输出。

10
00:00:56,807 --> 00:01:02,047
At execution, the robot carries out robot actions and receives new sensory observations.
执行时机器人输出动作，并接收新的感知观测。

11
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:08,020
Each of five tasks uses one hundred fifty robot and one thousand human demonstrations.
五项任务各150条机器人、1000条人类示范。

12
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:12,580
Each method is evaluated ten times per task on the physical robot.
每种方法每任务进行10次真机评测。

13
00:01:13,136 --> 00:01:19,256
The reported average is seventy percent, compared with twenty-nine for the retrained T-Rex baseline.
报告平均70%，对应重训T-Rex基线29%。

14
00:01:19,576 --> 00:01:25,036
Here, the metric awards partial credit for completed stages rather than counting only complete tasks.
这里按完成阶段给部分分数，并非只数完整成功。

15
00:01:25,606 --> 00:01:30,626
Separating a page earns point three; flipping multiple pages earns point seven.
分离纸页得0.3分，翻多页得0.7分。

16
00:01:31,006 --> 00:01:36,066
Only correctly flipping a single page earns one, so an average score is not full success.
正确翻一页才得1分，平均得分不等于完整成功率。

17
00:01:36,695 --> 00:01:42,235
Removing future tactile prediction reduces the average score to forty-two under this protocol.
移除未来触觉预测，同协议平均分降到42。

18
00:01:42,835 --> 00:01:49,955
The evidence supports contact-aware representation learning, with small evaluation counts and explicitly partial-credit outcomes.
证据支持接触表征学习，但试验少且需保留计分定义。
